# Stage one melee attack whose attack roll is pinned from outside, so
# tools/check_natural_one_attack.sh can read the engine's own verdict for a
# forced natural 1, 2 and 20 (bd inc-bp2y).
#
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/orc-mage-seed1-opt0822.sav \
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOF_FORCE_ROLL=1 \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/natural-one-attack.keys 1
#
# Read the result with tools/check_natural_one_attack.sh, which is what
# asserts; this file only produces the session.
#
# THE SUBJECT is the frozen orc mage of tools/fixtures/chars/orc-mage-seed1-
# opt0822.sav (Melee +3). "Natural One Attack Test God" (tools/fixtures/
# natural-one-attack-god.irh, spliced onto a scratch module by the check)
# grants +30 to hit on joining, so 3 + 30 = +33 beats any summoned goblin's
# Defense even on a forced roll of 1. The defect is therefore load-bearing:
# the arithmetic alone hits, and only the natural-1 clause can miss.
#
# THE ORACLE is the game's own attack line in the message log --
# "Attack: 1d20 (n) ... vs. Def D [hit|miss]" (src/Fight.cpp) -- which
# OPT_STORE_ROLLS keeps in the scrolling history. 'v' opens the history and
# @dump:messages photographs it; the check reads the [hit|miss] verdict off
# that line. INCURSION_LOF_FORCE_ROLL pins the d20 (src/Fight.cpp's
# LOFInitForcedRoll), so one run per forced value covers each case.
#
# Freeze Monsters (the eleventh row of the Wizard Mode Switches list) stops
# the goblin acting, so the only Attack line in the log is the player's own.
# The "Become Divine Champion" blessing grants the to-hit bonus; the ESC
# answers whatever the blessing's messages left open.

w
@expect "Enter wizard mode"
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC

w
@choose "Become Divine Champion"
"Natural One Attack Test God" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT
ENTER

# One melee blow at the goblin one square east.
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:attacked

v
@dump:messages
@while "Messages" ESC
@quit
